  "design_rationale": "First-order self-draining heater with long lag. Feedforward 0.322 centers output at target 0.5 from bracketing equilibria (u=0.3->0.469 settled slope 0, u=0.34->0.526 slope 0.0001) with incremental gain 1.425 (0.057/0.04). PI corrects residual: Kp=0.7 gives loop gain ~1.0 with K~1.2-1.4, stable against 15-40s dead-time and tau 150-250s. Ki=0.01 (Ti=70s) trims FF error within settling window; gated to 20% when |e|>0.15 to avoid windup during cold heat-up. D on filtered measurement Kd=8 with 20s filter damps lag overshoot, clamped to +/-0.12 for noise. Filter tau 12s smooths 0.005-0.01 noise. Integral clamp +/-0.25 leaves 0.25 authority, >3x max expected FF error 0.02-0.05, so no permanent offset. Output capped 0.75 plus yf>0.7/0.8 cutback keeps y far from 0.85 soft / 0.9 hard cutoff.",
  "machine_card": "Electric heater, positive gain: more power = hotter. Self-draining: u=0 falls from 0.544 to 0.319 in 180s still falling -0.0011/s, ambient <=0.2 likely ~0.04-0.15. No dead-zone: u=0.3-0.5 all move. Lag: flat 15-40s after steps (E1 15s, E2 ~25s, E3 ~40s) + dominant tau ~150-250s (180s holds not fully settled except after 360s at 0.3). Gain: incremental 1.42 between 0.3/0.34 equilibria, average ~0.7-0.9 from 0.2 baseline. Steady points: (u=0.3,y=0.469 slope 0), (u=0.34,y=0.526 slope 0.0001), (u=0.5,y~0.50-0.52 still rising 0.0007 after 180s). Hold for target 0.5 needs u~0.322 interpolated. Noise on y ~0.005-0.01. Speed: worst-case 0.006/s per u, observed avg ~0.001-0.002/s.",
