 "change_summary": "Lowered proportional kick (Kp 0.7->0.5 with +-0.25 clamp) and derivative (Kd 8->4, clip +-0.10, Td 20->15, Tf 12->10) to add phase margin for larger lag; strengthened integral (Ki 0.01->0.028, limits +-0.20, reduced when |e|>0.12) with conditional anti-windup to recover from post-overshoot droop without windup; kept nominal feedforward 0.322+0.70*(target-0.5) but made it adaptive by slowly transferring settled integral into ff (lam=0.005*dt when |e|<0.05) and tracking target changes; raised Umax 0.75->0.80 with P-clamp so effective cold-start drive is ~0.55 not 0.65 (less stored heat) but high power remains available if gain falls; kept 0.70/0.80 safety caps.",
 "design_rationale": "Slower lag leaves steady-state unchanged so fixed ff 0.322 remains correct on average but transient needs less aggressive P and better-damped D. Smaller Kp + P-clamp reduces heat stored during 100-150s rise that later appears as 0.09 overshoot. Smaller Kd with shorter Td still brakes rise but does not amplify delay-induced phase lag. Larger Ki removes the long 0.47-0.49 tail that caused most out-of-band time after 500s, while conditional integration and saturation freeze prevent windup during the initial 0.45 error. Adaptive ff learns u_ss online (u~0.29-0.32 for 0.5) so both nominal (u_ss~0.32) and changed plant are held without permanent integral offset, and target-shift logic preserves nominal behavior if target moves. Safety caps guarantee no soft-limit violation.",
