  "change_summary": "Kept feedforward+PI structure but retuned for ~+45s delay and ~1.8x tau: lowered Kp to 0.55 and Ki to 0.014 with tight anti-windup (+/-0.15), replaced raw D with lead-compensated P on predicted y (Tp=35s, y_pred=yf+Tp*df, p=Kp*(target-y_pred)) to brake early despite delay, kept Tf=8s/Td=12s filtering and 0.80/0.70/0.80 safety caps, and made feedforward slowly adapt to u when |e|<0.04 and |df|<0.001 with bumpless transfer. This damps delay-induced overshoot/limit-cycle while still heating aggressively when far and re-learning u_ss if gain drifts.",
  "design_rationale": "Delay increase cannot be fixed by higher integral - it causes hunting. Fix is phase lead: control predicted y 35s ahead, lower loop gain, filter derivative, freeze/slow integral when far or saturated, and adapt ff only when settled. Tp=35s compensates ~70s new dead-time without over-leading nominal 25s plant (still stable, slightly overdamped). Ki 0.014 gives ~2x phase margin vs old 0.028. I limits prevent windup during 200s warmup. ff adaptation recovers correct bias 0.32 nominal or new value without fighting integral.",
